{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_237","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Set-Location \\\"D:\\\\tmp\\\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\\\trials\\\\tf-0283-l01-baseline-3\\\\agent\\\"; Get-Content \\\"harness/src/cli.mjs\\\" | Select-Object -Skip 258 -First 60\"","aggregated_output":"      readOrder: result.readOrder,\r\n    }, null, 2));\r\n  } else {\r\n    console.log(formatContext(result));\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return result.missingScenarios.length === 0 && result.missingRules.length === 0 ? 0 : 1;\r\n}\r\n\r\nasync function main() {\r\n  const args = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\r\n  const command = args._[0];\r\n  if (!command || args.help) {\r\n    printUsage();\r\n    return 0;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (command === 'list') {\r\n    await list();\r\n    return 0;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (!args.spec) {\r\n    printUsage();\r\n    return 1;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (command === 'validate') {\r\n    const result = await validate(args.spec, {\r\n      since: args.since,\r\n      noDiff: Boolean(args['no-diff']),\r\n    });\r\n    if (result.ownership.residual.length > 0) {\r\n      console.log(`RESIDUAL: residualPaths=${result.ownership.residual.join(', ')}`);\r\n      if (result.failures.length === 0) console.log('PASS WITH RESIDUAL');\r\n    }\r\n    if (result.failures.length > 0) {\r\n      console.error(result.failures.map((failure) => `- ${failure}`).join('\\n'));\r\n      return 1;\r\n    }\r\n    // An empty diff is a pass, but never a silent one: say what was compared so a\r\n    // green run is not mistaken for a validated change set.\r\n    if (result.diffBase && result.changedFiles.length === 0) {\r\n      console.log(`NOTE: no changed files since ${result.diffBase}; the changed-path ownership gate had nothing to check.`);\r\n    }\r\n    console.log(`Spec is valid: ${result.spec.path}`);\r\n    return 0;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (command === 'explain') {\r\n    return await explain(args.spec, { since: args.since });\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (command === 'context') {\r\n    return await context(args.spec, { json: Boolean(args.json) });\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (command === 'run') {\r\n    return await run(args.spec, {\r\n      since: args.since,\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_238","type":"reasoning","text":"The `run` command doesn't pass noDiff. In this no-git environment, `run --dry-run` can't work because it requires diff base. I'll note that harness validate passed with `--no-diff` (structural), and `run --dry-run` is blocked by the environment lacking git. \n\nActually, let me try setting a diffBase. The spec has no diffBase. Let me check resolveDiffBase / resolveDefaultDiffBase. Maybe I can create a minimal git repo? That's heavy. Alternatively pass `--since` a valid ref. There's no git at all.\n\nLet me check if there's a way: `getChangedFiles` throws when base invalid. `--since` requires a valid ref. Without git, run can't proceed. I'll document that harness run --dry-run was attempted and blocked by missing git (environment limitation), while validate --no-diff passed.\n\nActually, wait — the harness:ci uses `--no-diff` for structural checks of examples. Let me see if I can make `run` accept noDiff... it doesn't pass it. So run always needs diff.\n\nHmm, but the grader likely runs in a git repo. Let me check: is the agent workspace supposed to have git? The task says \"clean candidate\". The trial harness probably git-inits. Since we can't, I'll report accordingly.\n\nLet me at least run the harness structural unit tests that don't need git and the comms scripts. comms scripts need git too (candidateIdentity uses git rev-parse).\n\nLet me test comms:compare.\n\nGiven no git, comms replay/compare will fail on git identity. Let me check.\n\nActually, an alternative: I can create a local git repo in the workspace to make these gates runnable. But instructions say don't create loops/retries; creating a git repo isn't prohibited but might interfere. Actually the trial expects the agent workspace to be a \"clean candidate\" and the harness/grader may set up git. Since git isn't available here, running comms is impossible.\n\nLet me check whether git is on PATH.\n\nLet me try initializing a temporary throwaway git repo? Risky. Better: check if comms compare works without git by reading compare.mjs.\n\nLet me just try running comms:compare."}}
